  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1227 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nBy later this week, the upper level ridge will re-establish \nitself over the eastern half of Texas and strengthen. Although the\nridge will be centered over eastern Texas, the western side of \nthe ridge will extend into west-central Texas. Although we will \nhave some low end (20%) chances for precipitation along our \nwestern CWA border Thursday into Saturday, the bulk of any showers\nand storms are expected to affect areas from the Big Bend \nnorthward into eastern New Mexico and the Texas Panhandle region. \nBy this weekend, the ridge is expected to weaken again, \npotentially bringing better rain chances back in the area early \nnext week. Temperatures will remain well above normal through this\ntime period with highs mainly in the 90s, and lows in the upper \n60s to mid 70s. Normal highs and lows at this time are in the \nmid/upper 80s and lower 60s.",
